{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeCellular","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeTypeAPresentationEquiv","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedRSKBurnside","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.NumSYTBridge","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasisCore","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.DivisionRing"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.span_murphySum_one_conjugates_eq_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.span_murphySum_one_conjugates_eq_top","kind":"theorem","line":532,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L532-L551","doc":"**Step 2: the one-column Murphy elements already span `H_n(q)`.**\n\n`{T_u · x_{(1ⁿ)} · T_v}` spans, because `x_{(1ⁿ)} = 1` and the `T_w` are a basis: take `u = 1`\nand the family already contains every `T_v`. So the row-standard Murphy family spans as soon as\nthe `T_w` do, and **the whole of the spanning input to `basisOfSpanning` is Lemma 3.14's\nstraightening** — moving a row-standard pair to standard pairs of dominating shape.\n\nStated over the conjugating pair rather than over tableaux precisely because the row-standard\ntableau type does not exist yet (see the section note): this is the algebraic content, and it\ndoes not have to wait for the indexing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphySum_singleton_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphySum_singleton_one","kind":"theorem","line":524,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L524-L530","doc":"**The trivial Young subgroup contributes `1`.** `x_{(1ⁿ)} = Σ_{w ∈ {1}} T_w = T_1 = 1`.\n\nThe one-column shape `(1ⁿ)` has every row of length one, so its row stabiliser is trivial and\nits Murphy element is the identity — which is what makes step 2 of the spanning argument free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyFamily_linearIndependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyFamily_linearIndependent","kind":"theorem","line":484,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L484-L492","doc":"Linear independence given spanning — the (C1) half the `Triangular` route was meant to\nsupply. Same standing caveat as `murphyBasisOfSpanning`: it proves `spans → independent`, and\nsays nothing about whether the family spans. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyBasisOfSpanning","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyBasisOfSpanning","kind":"def","line":468,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L468-L482","doc":"**The Murphy basis, given Mathas' spanning lemma (Thm 3.20).**\n\nSpanning goes in as an explicit hypothesis and the `Module.Basis` comes out, derived from it\ntogether with `murphyIndex_fintypeCard` and `finrank_eq_factorial`. The conclusion is not\namong the hypotheses, so this is a derivation, not an assumption dressed as infrastructure.\n\nWhat it does **not** claim: that anything spans. `murphyFamily` is now measured full rank at\n`n = 3, 4, 5` (see its docstring), so the hypothesis is at least satisfiable-looking, but\nLemma 3.14 is the open input and this lemma is silent about it —\n\"conditional-proved ≠ premise-established\". `basisOfSpanning` above is the same statement for\nan arbitrary family, and is the form to reach for when the family is not yet fixed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.basisOfSpanning","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.basisOfSpanning","kind":"def","line":454,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L454-L466","doc":"**(C1) modulo spanning** — Murphy's basis theorem, reduced to its one open input.\n\nA family indexed by `MurphyIndex (n + 1)` that spans `H_n(q)` **is** a basis, because the\nindex set has exactly `finrank` elements. Stated for an arbitrary family `m` so that the\nreduction is visibly independent of what `m` is; `murphyBasisOfSpanning` specialises it to\n`murphyFamily`. Nothing here assumes the conclusion: spanning goes in, a `Basis` comes out,\nand the bridge between them is `murphyIndex_fintypeCard` + `finrank_eq_factorial`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyIndex_fintypeCard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyIndex_fintypeCard","kind":"theorem","line":448,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L448-L452","doc":"`#MurphyIndex n = n!` as a `Fintype.card` — the `Nat.card` form is `murphyIndex_card`.\nThis is Mathas' `|M| = Σ_λ |Std(λ)|² = n!`, transported along RSK. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.instFintypeMurphyIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.instFintypeMurphyIndex","kind":"instance","line":445,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L445-L446","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyFamily","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyFamily","kind":"def","line":419,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L419-L443","doc":"The family `m_{st}` built from `murphyM`, indexed by `MurphyIndex (n + 1)` — a partition\nof `n + 1` with an ordered pair of standard tableaux of that shape, which is Murphy's index\nset. The two `StandardYoungTableau` types in the corpus are reconciled by\n`NumSYTBridge.toBraidKnotSYT`, and the filling by `SpechtStandardBasis.sytToTableau`.\n\n**Corrected 2026-08-31.** `murphyM` previously summed over `youngSubgroup n h t` —\nthe *second tableau's own* row stabiliser, a different conjugate subgroup for each `t`,\nwhere Murphy's `x_λ` is **one fixed** subgroup for every pair of the shape. That family was\nrank-deficient at every `n` tested (`5/6`, `23/24`, `117/120`), so it could not span and was\nnot Murphy's family. It now sums over the reference tableau's row stabiliser.\n\nThe guard that caught it is `run_rank_guard` in\n`computations/hecke/murphy_supp_rsk_probe.py` (exact arithmetic at `q = 7`): the fixed-`x_λ`\nfamily is full rank `6/6`, `24/24`, `120/120`. **That is evidence, not proof** — it says the\nspanning hypothesis below is no longer measured *unsatisfiable*, not that it holds for all\n`n`, which is Mathas' Lemma 3.14 and still open.\n\nNote the reference tableau itself is a red herring: `colSuperstandard` (column-major) is as\ngood as Murphy's row-superstandard `t^λ` — both are full rank. The subgroup was the defect.\nAudit: `docs/audits/2026-08-31-murphy-basis-triangular-lever-refuted.md` §3-ter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.lead_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.lead_injective","kind":"theorem","line":359,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L359-L364","doc":"**`lead_inj`** — cellular axiom (C1)'s first `Triangular` field, discharged.\n\nNo combinatorial content: `lead` is an `Equiv`, so injectivity is `Equiv.injective`. The work was\nin identifying the right map, not in proving this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.lead","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.lead","kind":"def","line":352,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L352-L357","doc":"**`lead`** — the leading permutation of a Murphy basis element, taken to be its RSK image.\n\nLanding in `Equiv.Perm (Fin n)` is forced: it is the index type of the `T_w` basis, hence of the\ncoordinate vectors `Triangular` quantifies over. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyIndexEquivPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyIndexEquivPerm","kind":"def","line":346,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L346-L350","doc":"**`MurphyIndex n ≃ S_n`** — the Robinson–Schensted correspondence, stated on the index type\nthe Murphy family actually uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyIndexEquivRSKCodomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyIndexEquivRSKCodomain","kind":"def","line":331,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L331-L344","doc":"**The index bridge**: RSK's codomain is `MurphyIndex n`, re-indexed.\n\n`{X : Σ μ, SYT μ × SYT μ // X.1.cells.card = n} ≃ MurphyIndex n`, by `subtypeSigmaEquiv` then\n`partitionShapeEquiv`. Both steps are already used, for their cardinality shadow only, inside\n`QOU.Mathlib.card_pairs_eq_sum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.repr_murphySum_one_of_subgroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.repr_murphySum_one_of_subgroup","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L290-L300","doc":"**`T_1` appears in `x_S` with coefficient `1`** whenever `S` is a subgroup — in particular for\na Young subgroup, since `1 ∈ S_λ`.\n\nThis is the candidate leading term: every `x_λ` has a distinguished unit coefficient, which is\nwhat a triangularity argument needs at the diagonal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.repr_murphySum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.repr_murphySum","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L274-L288","doc":"**The coordinates of `x_S` in the `T_w` basis are the indicator of `S`.**\n\nImmediate, because `x_S = ∑_{w ∈ S} T_w` is a sum of *distinct* basis vectors — but it is the\ncomputation every later coefficient argument starts from. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyM_colSuperstandard_diag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyM_colSuperstandard_diag","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L250-L260","doc":"**The anchor: `m_{t^λ t^λ} = x_λ`.** Both conjugating factors are `1`, so the reference pair\nof the Murphy family is the Murphy element itself — the base case of the dominance induction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyM_colSuperstandard_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyM_colSuperstandard_left","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L241-L248","doc":"**`m_{t^λ, t}` drops its left factor.** `d(t^λ) = 1`, so `T_{d(t^λ)}^* = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.dAt_colSuperstandard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.dAt_colSuperstandard","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L236-L239","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyIndex_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyIndex_card","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L212-L224","doc":"**`#MurphyIndex n = n!`** — the index type has exactly the dimension of `H_{n-1}(q)`.\n\n`Nat.card` of a sigma of pairs is `∑_p (#SYT p)²`, which is the RSK/Burnside identity. So the\nMurphy family is indexed by a type of exactly the right size, and (C1) — `Module.Basis\n(MurphyIndex (n+1)) K (H_n q)` — is a well-posed claim whose two halves each imply the other. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.instFiniteMurphyIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.instFiniteMurphyIndex","kind":"instance","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L209-L210","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.MurphyIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.MurphyIndex","kind":"def","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L202-L207","doc":"**The Murphy index**: a partition of `n`, with an ordered pair of standard tableaux of that\nshape. Exactly the data `murphyM` takes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyIndex_card_eq_finrank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyIndex_card_eq_finrank","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L180-L189","doc":"**The Murphy index set has exactly `dim_K H_n(q)` elements.**\n\nThe left side counts pairs of standard tableaux of a common shape — the `(s,t)` indexing\n`murphyM` — via the RSK/Burnside identity; the right is the Hecke algebra's dimension. Their\nagreement is what makes (C1) a one-sided question. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.murphyM","kind":"def","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L144-L156","doc":"**Murphy's `m_{st}`**, at last definable: `T_{d(s)}^* · x_λ · T_{d(t)}`, with `*` the\ntransported cellular anti-involution and `x_λ` the Murphy element of `t`'s Young subgroup.\n\nThis is a *definition*, not a theorem. That the `m_{st}` form a basis is cellular axiom (C1)\nand remains open; so does (C3). What has changed is that both can now be *written down* —\nevery ingredient is a named object rather than something to be built first. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.dAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.dAt","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L138-L142","doc":"`d(t)` at the Hecke algebra's index — `dOf t` transported along `μ.card = n + 1`, the same\nre-indexing `youngSubgroup` uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.antiAutTw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.antiAutTw","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L129-L136","doc":"**The cellular anti-involution, transported to the `T_w` presentation.**\n\n`H → HoS → HoSᵐᵒᵖ → Hᵐᵒᵖ`, the outer two steps being `algEquiv` and its `AlgEquiv.op`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.dOf_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.dOf_injective","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L109-L115","doc":"`d` is injective: distinct tableaux of the same shape give distinct permutations. This is\nwhat will make the Murphy family indexed by *pairs of tableaux* rather than over-counted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.colSuperstandard_trans_dOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.colSuperstandard_trans_dOf","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L102-L107","doc":"**The defining property of `d(t)`**: transporting the reference tableau along `d(t)`\nrecovers `t`. This is what makes `d` the right object to conjugate `x_λ` by. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.dOf_colSuperstandard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.dOf_colSuperstandard","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L96-L99","doc":"`d(t^λ) = 1`: the reference tableau is carried to itself by the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.dOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.dOf","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L89-L93","doc":"**`d(t)`** — the permutation of labels carrying the column-superstandard reference tableau\n`t^λ` to `t`. A composite of two `Equiv`s, since a tableau *is* an `Equiv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.σ_mul_murphySum_young","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.σ_mul_murphySum_young","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L63-L74","doc":"**Murphy's `x_λ` is a `q`-eigenvector, for the Young subgroup of an actual tableau.**\n\n`σ_i · x_λ = q · x_λ` whenever `s_i` lies in the (transported) row stabiliser of `t`. This is\nthe defining property of `x_λ`, now stated about the combinatorial object it is supposed to be\nabout rather than about an abstract subgroup. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.youngSubgroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung.youngSubgroup","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphyYoung.lean#L54-L61","doc":"**The Young subgroup of a tableau, at the Hecke algebra's index.**\n\n`Specht.rowStab t` lives over `Fin (Specht.nOf μ)`; `h : Specht.nOf μ = n + 1` transports it to\n`Fin (n + 1)`, where `IwahoriHecke K q n` acts. Pure re-indexing — `Equiv.permCongrHom` is a\n`MulEquiv`, so the image is a subgroup isomorphic to `rowStab t`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}